          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 607,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:8.05.100:block:1",
          "start": 81
        },
        "quote": "(b) Automatic dialing devices designed to transmit signals directly to the Police Department are prohibited for any but governmental agencies. Such automatic dialing devices may be interconnected to a special trunk line into the Police Department. Before such a device is interconnected to a special trunk line, the person performing this operation shall first obtain instructions from the Police Department concerning the procedure to be followed. The Police Department shall designate the number to be used for this purpose.",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:8.05.100:block:1#text",
        "unavailable_reason": null
      },
      {
        "artifact": "normalized_text",
        "availability": "available",
        "label": "TMC 8.05.100 block 2",
        "locator": {
          "block_index": 2,
          "component_id": "ede90cc2-206a-566d-b293-4f32edc3e8f2",
          "convention": "utf8_char_offset",
          "end": 872,
          "source_component_key": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:8.05.100:block:2",
          "start": 608
        },
        "quote": "(c) The owner or lessee of any automatic dialing device which is allowed to be connected to a special trunk line transmitting directly into the Police Department shall pay all telephone company charges connected therewith. (Code 1981 § 34-142. Code 1995 § 62-111.)",
        "ref_id": "ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:8.05.100:block:2#text",
